*.notes.md
*.plan.md
.claude/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- evidence corpus
# The raw pages, PDFs and model-response caches the ingestion pipeline builds.
# This repository ships the extracted facts and their verbatim quotes, not the
# source bodies they were quoted from: those are third-party government content
# and are not ours to redistribute. See NOTICE.
#
# Point ARIANE_CORPUS_DIR at a local corpus to run `pnpm gates:corpus`.
.ingest/
.firecrawl/
.corpus/
.private/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- data plane
# The private graph. Compiled bundles and the evidence behind them, fetched with
# `pnpm data:sync` and never committed:
#
#   .graph/*.json           the bundles, and jurisdictions.json
#   .graph/research/*.json  the extracted facts and the quote behind each one
#
# Three reasons, and the first is the one that decides it. These are third-party
# government pages and their extracts, and republishing them is not ours to do;
# see NOTICE. They are also 14MB, which put a 150,000 line diff in front of
# every reviewer and made a data correction look like a code change. And the
# database is where they actually live, so a checked-in copy is a fourth place
# to be wrong.
#
# Public tests use fixtures/demo, which is four invented nodes. See
# packages/core/src/data/providers.ts for how the three planes are chosen.
.graph/
# Older name for the same thing, so a stale clone does not commit one.
packages/core/src/data/graph/

# What the ingestion pipeline hands a human to look at: geocoder near-misses,
# rejected matches, the reasons. Regenerated by the run that produced it and
# stale the moment the data moves, so it is a working note, not a source file.
artifacts/

